      "response_text": " ```python\ndef is_throttled(history: list[float], window_sec: float, max_count: int, now: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if MORE than max_count events fall within the sliding window.\n\n    The window is the same half-open range used everywhere else in this module:\n    (now - window_sec, now]. An event at exactly now - window_sec is OUTSIDE\n    the window and is NOT counted. An event at exactly `now` IS counted.\n\n    Exactly `max_count` events in the window is allowed (returns False).\n    More than `max_count` returns True.\n\n    Args:\n        history: list of past event timestamps, sorted ascending.\n        window_sec: window length in seconds.\n        max_count: threshold; throttling kicks in at max_count + 1.\n        now: current time.\n    \"\"\"\n    threshold = now - window_sec\n    recent = [t for t in history if t > threshold]\n    return len(recent) > max_count\n```",
